        "original_id": "056f9cb2-6535-53b8-bb51-07f7fe84925e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Union Pacific Railroad, Clinchfield Railroad, Chesapeake and Ohio Railway\n- Places: Dante, Virginia, Elkhorn City, Sandy Ridge Mountains\n- Products: Challengers\n\nFacts:\n- In 1915, the Clinchfield Railroad completed a 35-mile segment from Dante, Virginia, to Elkhorn City.\n- The 1915 Clinchfield Railroad segment opened coal lands north of Sandy Ridge Mountains.\n- The 1915 Clinchfield Railroad segment formed a connection with the Chesapeake and Ohio Railway at Elkhorn City.\n- Challengers were most common on the Union Pacific Railroad and the Clinchfield Railroad.",
